  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Asenapine is an atypical antipsychotic given for schizophrenia and for manic episodes linked to bipolar disorder. It is an approved medicine with an authorised product in the European Union, though it carries a boxed warning.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q416545\">Wikidata Q416545</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>asenapine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>N05AH05</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB06216\">DB06216</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/11954293\">11954293</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:71255\">71255</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q416545\">Q416545</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C21H20ClNO5</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>401.843 g/mol (PubChem CID 11954293)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>3.8 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table><p><small>Drugs.Common 25.09 gave 285.8 g/mol (-28.9 %); replaced by the value above</small></p></body></html>"));
